It is Sunday evening.
Someone knocks on the door.
Bruno is sleeping in his basket, but he wakes up immediately.
He hears Sabine's voice outside.
He runs happily to the door.
I open the door and Sabine comes in.
"Hello Maya!" says Sabine cheerfully.
"Hello, my little Bruno!"
"Well, are you a good dog?"
"He did everything great," I answer.
"We went to the park together."
"At home I threw his toy, and he always brought it back."
"I fed him on time."
"I gave him nothing from my dinner."
Sabine laughs.
"Thank you very much for your help, Maya," she says.
She picks the small dog up and takes his bag.
Sabine takes him home with her.
My flat is very quiet now.
